;;; `open` written as an object's name loads, as an object —
;;; regression `is-a-object`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `(is-a open Thing)` types `open` as an object of `Thing`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `open` is a name wherever the kernel does not read it, at the head of a
;;; written fact, a premise or a conclusion, and under an ordinary relation the
;;; head of a fact the kernel does not read (Q-M1f.66, Q-M1f.571): here it is
;;; written as an object's name, so the program loads, and every command
;;; answers.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `f62e34e1`, release: the program loads, and the blind enumerator proposes
;;; `(a open)`, `(p open)` and `(q open)`: R is 32 states, exit 0 on every
;;; command.
;;; The engine loads it.

(relation a Thing :why "{?3} is an a")
(relation p Thing :why "{?3} is a p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?3} is a q")
(is-a k Thing)
(a k)
(is-a open Thing)
